          {
            "id": "p1",
            "locator": "Ledger Secrets section",
            "text": "The Ledger Secret symmetric key is used to encrypt and protect the integrity (using AES-GCM) of all write transactions executed by the service and recorded in the ledger."
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "locator": "Algorithms and Curves section",
            "text": "Authenticated encryption in CCF relies on AES256-GCM. Ledger authentication relies on Merkle trees using SHA2-256."
          }
        ],
